          "text": "CPU Memory Hierarchy\n\nDRAM Behind Cache: Why DRAM is Slow?\n  Weak storage signal\n DRAM stores bits as tiny capacitor charges, producing only a small voltage\n  difference on long bitlines.\n  Sensing takes time\n  The sense amplifier must detect and amplify a very small voltage change\n   into a full 0/1 value.\n  Destructive read\n  Reading a DRAM cell disturbs its stored charge, so the data must be\n  restored after every row activation.\n  Large dense arrays\n DRAM prioritizes capacity and cost per bit, so rows/bitlines are long and\n  have higher RC delay.\n  Solution: Multi-Bank, Multi-Rank DRAM\n\n\n\n\nMemory Wall     CPU Memory    GPU Memory    SOTA Memory     Advanced AI Computing and Systems        35",
